<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Nineveh (627)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/627">627 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-sasanian-war-of-602-628">Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> was fought in 627 CE near the ruins of ancient Nineveh in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, where the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> defeated a Sasanian army. It was the climax of the Byzantine-Sasanian war of 602–628. The defeat led to the overthrow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> and a succession crisis that left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> exhausted on the eve of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Arab conquests</a>.</p></div>
